  "findings": {
    "P0": [],
    "P1": [
      {
        "id": "H12-P1-1",
        "status": "FIXED",
        "title": "Imported-video target tap was never persisted",
        "detail": "The mandatory gate step 'taps target -> target persists' was not met: the tap lived only in AnalyzeScreen React state (targetSeed) and was passed to runCaptureAnalysis, which returns 'unavailable' for imported clips before persisting anything \u2014 the user's tap was silently discarded on every imported video. Fix: new local_capture.target_seed column (additive migration in apps/mobile/src/data/db.ts), setCaptureTargetSeed/getCaptureTargetSeed in apps/mobile/src/data/repository.ts (owner-scoped, corrupt rows read as null, never reconstructed), wired into AnalyzeScreen.scoreCapture before analysis. Regression tests: apps/mobile/__tests__/importedTargetSeed.test.ts (4 tests)."
      },
      {
        "id": "H12-P1-2",
        "status": "UNRESOLVED_EXTERNALLY_BLOCKED",
        "title": "Imported videos never reach StrokeEvents or analysis \u2014 mandatory flow ends in honest abstention",
        "detail": "runCaptureAnalysis returns {kind:'unavailable', reason:'Imported videos have no recorded pose sequence yet. Record with the guided camera to get a Technique Score.'} for every captureMode==='imported_video' clip; the CapturedClip type for imports deliberately forbids poseSequence/trigger/captureEvidence (no live-capture metadata is assumed or fabricated \u2014 verified in assertCapturedClip). Consequence: the mandatory gate flow '... -> individual StrokeEvents -> analysis' is NOT implemented in this release candidate for imported video; the UI still walks the user through stroke declaration and target tap before surfacing the abstention (misleading-UX component of this finding; the tap is at least persisted now per H12-P1-1). Building the missing path requires on-device pose extraction over imported frames (iOS Vision / device hardware), which cannot be implemented or validated on this Linux environment. Not fixable internally without fabricating pose data, which is prohibited."
      }
    ],
    "P2": [
      {
        "id": "H12-P2-1",
        "status": "UNRESOLVED",
        "title": "Bit-flipped media passes the decode-deficit gate",
        "detail": "corrupt-bitflip.mp4 decodes all 360/360 declared frames with 7 decoder error lines, so the decoded_frame_deficit check (min fraction 0.9) does not trip and the capture envelope reads SUPPORTED. Downstream pose/quality gates would still have to catch visual corruption. Noted, not weakened."
      },
      {
        "id": "H12-P2-2",
        "status": "NOTED",
        "title": "Frame-duplicated synthetic slow motion is rejected as still_image_video",
        "detail": "ffmpeg setpts-based slow motion duplicates frames, so >=50% frozen pairs trips the OOD gate. True unique-frame 120fps slo-mo cannot be synthesized from a 30fps source; device slo-mo behavior needs iPhone media (external)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "not_measured": [
    "On-device iOS/Android import (native importVideo module, PhotoKit/copy path) \u2014 requires iPhone/Mac.",
    "True variable-frame-rate device recordings and real 120/240fps slo-mo \u2014 requires device media.",
    "End-to-end imported analysis \u2014 path does not exist in this RC (see H12-P1-2)."
  ],
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "rationale": "The ingestion half of the gate certifies cleanly on Linux with real media: 26/26 files handled without a crash, 17/17 playable files probed and measured correctly (rotation, VFR, HEVC, .mov, 4K, re-encodes), 9/9 corrupt/unsupported files failed gracefully with descriptive errors or closed-set reason codes, no live-capture metadata is assumed or fabricated for imports, and the target tap now persists (P1 fixed with regression tests). However the mandatory flow explicitly required by GATE 12 \u2014 imported video producing individual StrokeEvents and an analysis \u2014 is not implemented in this release candidate: every imported video terminates in an honest abstention. That is an honest, guided dead end rather than a silent failure, but a MANDATORY gate whose core flow cannot complete on any input cannot be certified PASS. Completing the path requires on-device pose extraction (iPhone/Mac), so remediation is externally blocked from this environment; the verdict is FAIL for the release candidate as it stands, with BLOCKED_EXTERNAL remediation."
}